    Across urban metropolises globally—from South Asia and Southeast Asia to European capitals—the two-wheeler is the true lifeblood of daily commuting. Millions of office workers, university students, and delivery couriers rely on motorcycles for intra-city mobility. But with petrol prices reaching historic highs, the burning question in 2026 is: <strong>Are electric motorcycles and scooters genuinely worth the investment?</strong>
  </p>
  
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    While electric cars often require 2 to 3 years to break even due to their large battery packs, the economics of <strong>electric two-wheelers</strong> are radically faster. In this guide, we break down initial purchase prices, recurring battery charging expenses, courier fleet savings, and common real-world limitations.
  </p>

