        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    For an everyday office commuter, switching to an electric two-wheeler puts <strong>75% to 80% of their monthly commuting budget</strong> directly back into their personal savings.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">2. The Delivery Courier Game-Changer</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Nowhere is the electric motorcycle revolution moving faster than in commercial food delivery and courier logistics (such as Uber Eats, Deliveroo, Bykea, Foodpanda, and Zomato).
  </p>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    A commercial courier regularly logs between <strong>80 to 120 kilometers every single day</strong>. At these high mileages, a petrol motorcycle burns significant fuel volume, requiring frequent motor oil changes every 1,500 kilometers.
  </p>
  <p class="mb-6 leading-relaxed">
    By switching to an electric bike with either a dual-battery setup or battery-swapping subscription, delivery riders routinely break even on their vehicle purchase in just <strong>6 to 9 months</strong>! From that point onward, their monthly operational take-home pay increases significantly.
  </p>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">3. Battery Swapping vs. Plug-in Home Charging</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    Unlike four-wheelers which rely almost exclusively on fixed battery packs, electric two-wheelers utilize two distinct refueling paradigms:
  </p>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6 not-prose">
    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200">
      <strong class="text-sm font-black text-gray-950 block mb-1">Fixed Battery (Home AC Charging)</strong>
      <p class="text-xs text-gray-600 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        Charges from any standard 220V/110V wall outlet in 3 to 4 hours. You own the battery outright and pay only your residential electricity tariff. Best for fixed-commute riders traveling under 60 km daily.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-emerald-50/70 border border-emerald-300">
      <strong class="text-sm font-black text-emerald-950 block mb-1">Removable Battery Swapping (BaaS)</strong>
      <p class="text-xs text-emerald-800 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        Pull into an automated kiosk, swap a depleted 10 kg battery pack for a 100% full battery in 60 seconds. You pay a monthly energy subscription without worrying about long-term battery degradation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-950 mt-10 mb-4">4. Real-World Limitations to Keep in Mind</h2>
  <p class="mb-4 leading-relaxed">
    While the financial advantages are overwhelming, prospective riders should evaluate three practical constraints:
  </p>
  <ul class="list-disc pl-5 mb-6 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold text-gray-800">
    <li><strong>Top Speed Limits:</strong> Entry-level electric bikes are electronically capped at 55 to 70 km/h (35-45 mph), which is ideal for city streets but inadequate for inter-city motorways.</li>
    <li><strong>Water Wading & Monsoon Flooding:</strong> Modern electric bikes carry IP67-rated waterproof battery enclosures and hub motors, but prolonged submersion in deep urban floodwaters can damage wiring harness terminals.</li>
    <li><strong>Battery Weight:</strong> If you live in an apartment on the third floor with no ground-floor outlet, carrying a 12 kg battery pack upstairs for charging requires physical effort.</li>
  </ul>

